      "title": "fix: skip tag-annotation fetch step on workflow_dispatch",
      "url": "https://github.com/remcovanmook/draft-ipv6-resolved-gateway/pull/1",
      "state": "MERGED",
      "author": "remcovanmook",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "The 'Get Tag Annotations' step runs:\r\n  git fetch -f origin ${{ github.ref }}:${{ github.ref }}\r\n\r\nWhen the workflow is triggered manually (workflow_dispatch), github.ref resolves to refs/heads/main. Git refuses to fetch into a branch that is already checked out, exiting with code 128.\r\n\r\nThe fetch is only meaningful for tag-triggered runs (it retrieves annotated tag metadata that the shallow checkout misses). Add an 'if: startsWith(github.ref, \"refs/tags/\")' condition so the step is skipped entirely on manual dispatch triggers.",
      "createdAt": "2026-04-30T12:20:19Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-30T12:31:50Z",
      "baseRepository": "remcovanmook/draft-ipv6-resolved-gateway",
